# Release audit policy

- Never push or deploy from a dirty working tree or an unaudited commit.
- Before proposing a push, run `npm run audit:prepush` and report failures.
- Treat access-control, XSS, SSRF, wrong-condition evidence, unsupported medical claims, dead citations, and private-artifact exposure as release blockers.
- Patient-visible content must use the server-sealed output; browser code must not invent claims or citations.
- Every bug fix requires a behavioral regression that fails on the defect.
- Do not weaken a failing assertion into a warning or bypass a gate to make CI pass.
- External live-link and production checks belong in scheduled/post-deploy jobs; deterministic safety checks must remain in the pre-push gate.
- A release is complete only when the deployed SHA matches the reviewed Git SHA and post-deploy smoke checks pass.
